workedExamples.solution_text:
The period is $2\pi/(\pi/5)=10$ hours.
Find the boundary times:
$\begin{aligned}2.5&=3-\cos\left(\frac{\pi t}{5}\right)\\\cos\left(\frac{\pi t}{5}\right)&=\frac12\end{aligned}$
For $0\le t\le10$:
$\frac{\pi t}{5}=\frac{\pi}{3}\quad\text{or}\quad\frac{5\pi}{3}$
$t=\frac53\quad\text{or}\quad t=\frac{25}{3}$
The sketch shows that the depth is at least $2.5$ metres between these crossings.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.8cm]
\definecolor{modelblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{thresholdred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.6,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,4.6);
\path (10.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$t$};
\path (0,4.6) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$d$};
\draw[modelblue,thick,domain=0:10,samples=101] plot (\x,{3-cos(36*\x)});
\draw[thresholdred,dashed] (0,2.5)--(10,2.5);
\draw[black,dotted] ({5/3},0)--({5/3},2.5);
\draw[black,dotted] ({25/3},0)--({25/3},2.5);
\fill[black] ({5/3},2.5) circle (1.2pt);
\fill[black] ({25/3},2.5) circle (1.2pt);
\path (0,2.5) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$2.5$};
\path ({5/3},0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\frac53$};
\path ({25/3},0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\frac{25}{3}$};
\path (10,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$10$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}\text{Duration}&=\frac{25}{3}-\frac53\\&=\frac{20}{3}\end{aligned}$
The depth is at least $2.5$ metres for $6$ hours $40$ minutes.
